{
  "version": "batch45b-kinetics-fresh-class-disjoint-gradient-vlm-strict-parser-20261102-v2",
  "enabled": true,
  "description": "Fresh TAP-Vid-Kinetics Kinetics-700-2020 validation holdout: 12 new video IDs from 12 new action classes, disjoint from Batch42 and prior manifest video IDs; 6 DEV / 6 TEST. Compare KLT, NCC, ORB affine proxy and Sobel-gradient identity gates; test local SmolVLM2-2.2B with marked query frame plus reference crop under a DEV-only admission gate. Preflight regression fixed: VLM parser now requires a full-string single-token label; explanatory prefixes/suffixes are invalid.",
  "source_of_truth": "GitHub main; runner freezes clean checkout SHA in .automation/state.json. Raw videos, shards, frames, private point tracks, predictions and model weights remain local on Tang.",
  "failure_policy": "Single attempt per frozen stage; fail closed. Preserve failed logs and partial downloads. Any repair requires a new GitHub source SHA and a new repo-batch*-tested directory. Never tune on TEST.",
  "test_policy": "Selection is deterministic and video/action-class disjoint from Batch42. CPU tracker selection and VLM admission use DEV only. CPU and VLM TEST predictions are SHA-pinned before one-time scoring. If the VLM DEV gate blocks, TEST VLM inference is skipped and the TEST VLM oracle is never opened.",
  "gpu_policy": "VLM inference stages use /tmp/tang_shared_gpu_experiments.lock; require no other CUDA compute process and at least 11,000 MiB free. CPU stages explicitly disable OpenCV OpenCL.",
  "data_policy": "Download only the 12 selected class shards from the official CVDF S3 path list. Preserve existing media and partial downloads. No video, frame, shard, private oracle, weight, generated media or secret may be committed.",
